  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement_Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the heart of Japan's bustling metropolis lies a serene world, where nature and technology coexist in perfect harmony. The Tokyo Forest Park is not just any green oasis; it's an extraordinary blend of urban life and natural beauty that has transformed the city's skyline.\\\\\nBuilt on a former railway station site, this 10-hectare park boasts lush forests, clear streams, and an array of exotic plant species that have been introduced to create a unique ecosystem. The Tokyo Forest Park is more than just a place for recreation; it's also home to several fascinating attractions, such as the Sky Tree Tower and the Japan Science Center & Planetarium.\\\\\nThe park offers visitors an opportunity to explore different ecosystems within a single day: from dense forests rich in wildlife to sun-drenched meadows and shaded walkways that provide refuge during the hottest summer months.\\\\\nThe Tokyo Forest Park is more than a park; it's an experience, where urban dwellers can escape to nature while still being close to city life.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of Tokyo Forest Park?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To provide a place for urban dwellers to escape nature.\",\n        \"To serve as an exclusive residential area.\",\n        \"To host major sporting events.\",\n        \"To construct a new railway station.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"To provide a place for urban dwellers to escape nature.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What feature of Tokyo Forest Park allows visitors to experience different ecosystems?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The Sky Tree Tower\",\n        \"A variety of fast-food restaurants\",\n        \"Different types of trees and plant species\",\n        \"An indoor amusement park\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Different types of trees and plant species\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"Which attraction is located within the Tokyo Forest Park?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The Tokyo Tower\",\n        \"The Japan Science Center & Planetarium\",\n        \"A water park\",\n        \"An aquarium\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"The Japan Science Center & Planetarium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is unique about the Tokyo Forest Park's ecosystem?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It has a large population of exotic birds.\",\n        \"It includes a variety of desert plant species.\",\n        \"It features an array of native Japanese trees and plants.\",\n        \"It is home to rare types of reptiles.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It has a unique blend of urban life and natural beauty\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"Which statement best describes the relationship between Tokyo Forest Park and its surroundings?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The park is isolated from city life.\",\n        \"The park complements urban living by providing a natural escape.\",\n        \"The park contrasts with the bustling metropolis, creating tension.\",\n        \"The park is an artificial addition to the existing urban landscape.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"The park complements urban living by providing a natural escape.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
